@* 
    This page explains what MiniMart is and what users can do on the site.
    It gives a simple overview of the app features and how it relates to the assignment.
*@

<section class="container" style="text-align:center; padding:2rem 0;">
    <h1>About Us</h1>
    <p class="lead">A lightweight ASP.NET Core MVC demo project for IS4439 Web Application Development.</p>

    @* Add the image under the title *@
    <img src="~/images/MiniMart_logo_font.svg"
         alt="MiniMart logo"
         style="max-width:600px; margin-top:1rem;" />
</section>


<article>
    <h2>What You Can Do</h2>
    <p>
        MiniMart is a simple web application that demonstrates the key features of an
        <strong>ASP.NET Core MVC</strong> site.
        It allows you to view, add, and inspect sample products in a mock online store environment.
    </p>

    <h3>Core Features</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>View Products:</strong> Browse a list of products, each with details like name, price, and stock status.</li>
        <li><strong>Add New Products:</strong> Use the Add Product form to create new items. Built-in validation ensures correct data.</li>
        <li><strong>View Details:</strong> Click any product to view its details on a dedicated page.</li>
        <li><strong>Routing & Navigation:</strong> The app uses both conventional and attribute routing for clean URLs.</li>
        <li><strong>Error Handling:</strong> Friendly 404 page styled with the same layout.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom Tag Helper:</strong> Demonstrates how a &lt;test&gt; tag can render as a link to an external site.</li>
    </ul>


    <p>
        This project was developed as part of the <strong>IS4439 Web Application Development</strong> module.
        It focuses on teaching routing, model binding, validation, layouts, and basic user interface design.
    </p>

   
</article>
